# Modular Python

Keep each Python file near 500 lines. A file that long is still one unit a reader can hold in mind. Past that, the next change belongs in its own module.

`BoundingBoxNavigator/BoundingBoxNavigator.py` is already well past that limit. New behavior goes in a new module under `BoundingBoxNavigator/`, imported by the existing module. Do not add features by extending that file.

If a change would push a file further past about 500 lines, split the new code out first.

If this check failed, fix it before pushing to `dev` or `main`.
